=== QX001 | a query built by joining a value into its text, then run
q:{[s] value "select from t where sym=`",s}

=== QX001 | the value converted on the way in is still spliced
q:{[t] value "select from ",string t}

=== clean | a constant query has nothing spliced into it
q:{value "select from t"}

=== clean | value on a name says nothing about where the text came from
q:{[s] value s}

=== clean | a conditional choosing between constant queries splices no data
h:value $[a;"{select from x}";"{x}"],"y",b

=== clean | a string that is not a query
r:value "1+",string 2

=== QX002 | a password written into the source
password:"hunter2"

=== QX002 | under a namespace, any of the usual spellings
.cfg.apiKey:"abc123"

=== clean | a prompt is a message, not a secret
passwordPrompt:"Enter password"

=== clean | read from the environment, where it belongs
password:getenv`PASS

=== clean | an empty string holds nothing
token:""

=== clean | a literal that is only part of the value: a delimiter, a prefix
f:{[x] token:"," vs x; token}
g:{[x] token:"Bearer ",x; token}

=== QX002 | the whole value, before a comment or inside a lambda
apiKey:"abc123" / rotate yearly
f:{secret:"s3cr3t"; secret}

=== QX001 | get evaluates a string as value does (q 5)
f:{get "select from t where a=",x}

=== QX001 | and a handle hands it to the remote .z.pg
g:{[h;x] h "select from t where a=",x}

=== clean | a constant query over a handle, and a joined string only shown
g:{[h] h "select from t"}
k:{show "select from t where a=",x}
